<main className={"view"}> <nav className={"secbar"} aria-label={"Physician writing"}> <div className={"wrap secbar__in"}> <p className={"secbar__k"}><a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/"}>{"Physician writing"}</a></p> <ul className={"secbar__l"}> <li className={"has-sub"}><button className={"sbtrig"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sbd-558"}>{"Papers "}<svg className={"chev"} viewBox={"0 0 12 12"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M2 4l4 4 4-4"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.7"} /></svg></button></li> <li className={"has-sub"}><button className={"sbtrig"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sbd-559"}>{"Support "}<svg className={"chev"} viewBox={"0 0 12 12"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M2 4l4 4 4-4"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.7"} /></svg></button></li> </ul> <a className={"secbar__cta"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Send the case "}<svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"} /></svg></a> </div> <div className={"sbdrop"} id={"sbd-558"} hidden={true}> <div className={"sbdrop__l"}> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/case-report/"}>{"Case report"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/original-research-article/"}>{"Original research article"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/physician-manuscripts/"}>{"Physician manuscripts"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/clinical-literature-review-for-an-evidence-based-medicine/"}>{"Clinical literature review"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"sbdrop"} id={"sbd-559"} hidden={true}> <div className={"sbdrop__l"}> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/research-proposal/"}>{"Research proposal"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/literature-search-and-citation/"}>{"Literature search & citation"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/customized-writing/"}>{"Customized writing"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/physician-training/"}>{"Physician training"}</a> </div> </div> </nav> <div className={"crumbar"}> <div className={"wrap"}> <p><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M3 10.2 12 3l9 7.2V20a1 1 0 0 1-1 1h-5v-6H9v6H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1z"} /></svg><a href={"/"} data-nav={""}>{"Home"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><a href={"/services/"}>{"Services"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/"}>{"Physician writing"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><em>{"Customized Medical Writing for Physicians"}</em></p> <span className={"crumbar__tag"}>{"Research that survives peer review"}</span> </div> </div> <section className={"phero"}> <div className={"wrap phero__in"}> <div> <h1>{"Customized Medical Writing for Physicians"}</h1> <div className={"prose"}> <p>{"Most of what a practising clinician has to write does not fit a service page. A departmental white paper, a CME module, a rebuttal letter, a conference talk, a patient-facing explainer, a medico-legal report, a publication plan for a whole year’s output — each in a different register, each governed by different rules, and each competing for the same absent evenings. This is where that work is written. It is also where we say plainly what we will not write, and why: assessed academic work submitted as somebody’s own is a criminal offence to provide in England and an offence to advertise in Australia, and no wording on a website changes that. Pubrica’s physician writers work within those limits, and say so plainly where a request falls outside them."}</p> </div> <div className={"hero__actions"}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#cw-auth"}>{"Check an author against the ICMJE criteria"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#fsm-cw"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-cw"}>{"See a sample"}</a> </div> </div> <figure className={"jmatch rv"} style={{ margin: "0" }}> <figcaption className={"jmatch__bar"}> <span><b>{"One document set at a glance"}</b>{" · a year’s output"}</span> <span>{"7 documents · 4 registers"}</span> </figcaption> <div className={"jmatch__body"}> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Written for the reader each one actually has"}</b><span>{"4 registers"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"One set of facts, checked once, reused"}</b><span>{"No drift"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Every contributor checked against ICMJE"}</b><span>{"Before drafting"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Assistance declared, with permission obtained"}</b><span>{"In writing"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Assessed academic work"}</b><span>{"Declined"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--no"} style={{ '--w': "12%" }} /></div> </div> </div> <div className={"jmatch__foot"}> <p className={"funnel"}><b>{"Brief"}</b> <i>{"→"}</i>{" register "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" facts "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" draft "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" review "}<i>{"→"}</i> <b>{"delivery"}</b></p> </div> </figure> </div> </section> <div className={"creds"}> <div className={"wrap creds__in"}> <span className={"creds__lab"}>{"Every document"}</span> <ul className={"creds__list"}> <li>{"Written to its own register"}</li> <li>{"Facts checked to source"}</li> <li>{"Authorship settled first"}</li> <li>{"Assistance declared"}</li> <li>{"No assessed work"}</li> </ul> </div> </div> <div className={"proof"}><div className={"wrap proof__in"}> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"From $180"}</b><span>{"A single document, in 4–7 business days"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"Since 2009"}</b><span>{"Writing for clinicians across every register they need"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"ICMJE · GPP 2022"}</b><span>{"With writing assistance disclosed, not concealed"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"ISO 9001:2015"}</b><span>{"Quality management certified · cert. H3CR9TCU20251212INDQM10N"}</span></div> </div></div> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Where the line is"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What we will not write, stated before you ask."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Every writing service has a boundary. Most keep it in the terms and conditions. Ours is here, because a client who finds out at the quote stage has wasted a week and a client who finds out afterwards has a bigger problem than that."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"prose rv rv-d1"} style={{ maxWidth: "none" }}> <p><b>{"We do not write theses, dissertations or any other assessed work to be submitted as a student’s own."}</b>{" This is not a house preference. In England, providing, arranging or advertising such a service is a criminal offence under sections 27 and 28 of the Skills and Post-16 Education Act 2022. In Australia, providing or advertising academic cheating services is an offence under the TEQSA Act as amended in 2020, with penalties of up to 500 penalty units and two years’ imprisonment. The QAA defines contract cheating as a third party completing work that a student then submits as their own where that input is not permitted, and notes it is not always a commercial transaction. Universities’ academic integrity regulations prohibit it and typically permit only limited, declared editing and proofreading."}</p> <p><b>{"What we do instead sits inside those boundaries, and the boundaries are your institution’s to draw."}</b>{" Language editing and proofreading to the extent your university permits, and declared where it requires declaration. Statistical analysis and its interpretation, as a named collaborator with authorship assessed on the criteria rather than assumed away. Conversion of an "}<i>{"already examined"}</i>{" thesis chapter into a journal article, which is a publication rather than an assessment and is a rewrite rather than a trim. Training and coaching on how to structure and write the work yourself, which is the thing most students actually need and almost nobody sells them. If you are unsure where your institution draws the line, ask your supervisor or research office before you ask us — and we will ask you what the answer was."}</p> <p><b>{"We also do not write to a conclusion."}</b>{" A brief that specifies the finding in advance is not a writing brief. We will write a persuasive document arguing a position you hold, with the evidence for it and the counter-argument acknowledged; we will not write one that reports a result the data does not support, omits an inconvenient finding, or describes an association in the grammar of causation because that reads better. Where a document has industry sponsorship, GPP 2022 applies alongside the ICMJE, and the sponsor’s role — including in the writing of the report — is disclosed rather than managed."}</p> <p><b>{"And we do not write anything that has to conceal who wrote it."}</b>{" Declared assistance is legitimate; that is the whole distinction. If a document cannot carry an acknowledgement because acknowledging it would defeat its purpose, that document is the one we are declining."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"What we write"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Twelve kinds of document, in four different registers."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Register is the thing clients most often underestimate. The same clinical fact written for a journal, a regulator, a colleague and a patient is four genuinely different sentences, and a document written in the wrong register fails for reasons its author cannot see."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps caps--get rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Continuing education and training content"}</b> <span>{"Modules, case-based teaching, assessment items and facilitator material, written for an accredited provider to certify rather than certified by us — see our "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"#/physician-training"} data-nav={""}>{"physician training"}</a>{" page for exactly what that means and who may accredit what. Register: instructional, with the learning objective doing the work rather than the prose."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Conference talks, slides and speaker notes"}</b> <span>{"A fifteen-minute talk is not a compressed paper. It has one claim, three supporting points and a slide count that assumes somebody at the back is reading rather than listening. Built with speaker notes, timings, and the two slides an audience will ask about."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Rebuttal and response-to-reviewer letters"}</b> <span>{"Every comment triaged into concede, answer with evidence, or decline with a reason — and the third of those is the one authors avoid and editors expect. Written with the page and line of every change, and in a tone that does not cost you the editor. "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"/services/publication-support/responding-to-reviewers/"} data-nav={""}>{"Sold on its own here."}</a></span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Publication planning"}</b> <span>{"A year of output mapped: which papers a dataset supports and in what order, which meeting each abstract goes to, what depends on what, and where the authorship decisions sit. Under GPP 2022 where the research is company-sponsored, which adds requirements rather than removing them."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"White papers and position statements"}</b> <span>{"For a department, a society or a company. The genre’s failure mode is a document that reads as advocacy while claiming to be evidence; the fix is stating the position openly at the top and then arguing it honestly, including what the other side has right."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Medico-legal and expert reports"}</b> <span>{"Structured, referenced and written for a reader who is not clinical and will be cross-examined on it. The duty to the court, where one applies, is the expert’s alone; we structure, reference and edit, and we do not supply an opinion or sign anything."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Hospital and departmental reports"}</b> <span>{"Service evaluations, business cases, annual reviews and board papers. Register: a committee reading twelve papers in an evening. Recommendation first, evidence under it, and the ask stated as a number rather than implied."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Patient-facing material"}</b> <span>{"Leaflets, discharge instructions and explainers, written at a measured reading level rather than an asserted one. Our "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"#/patient-education-content"} data-nav={""}>{"patient education content"}</a>{" page covers this properly, including which instruments are used and what target they are measured against."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Grant and fellowship applications"}</b> <span>{"Written to the funder’s scoring criteria in the order and with the weight they publish, rather than adapted to them afterwards. "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"/services/research-services/grant-writing/"} data-nav={""}>{"Covered in full on the grant writing page."}</a></span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Regulatory and clinical study documents"}</b> <span>{"Protocols, clinical study reports, investigator brochures and clinical evaluation reports. A different discipline with its own conventions, and handled by the "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"/services/research-services/medical-writing/"} data-nav={""}>{"medical and regulatory writing"}</a>{" team rather than here."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Correspondence that matters"}</b> <span>{"A letter to an editor about a paper, a response to an integrity query, a cover letter for a difficult submission, a note to a collaborator about authorship. Short documents where the tone is the substance, and where a draft read by somebody outside the situation is worth more than the words."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Editing and rewriting anything above"}</b> <span>{"Often the better buy. Most drafts we receive are structurally sound and unclear about what they are claiming, and the work is to find the argument, put it at the front, and remove what is interesting to the author and irrelevant to the reader. Charged on what the document needs rather than on its length."}</span> </div> </div> </div> </section> <nav className={"pagenav"} aria-label={"On this page"}><div className={"wrap pagenav__in"}><a href={"#pn-customized-writing-who-we-serve-1vyhfoc"} aria-current={"true"}>{"Who we serve"}</a><a href={"#pn-customized-writing-how-it-works-18syixm"}>{"How it works"}</a><a href={"#pn-customized-writing-our-experts-1aaq5aj"}>{"Our experts"}</a><a href={"#pn-customized-writing-sample-work-ytogif"}>{"Sample work"}</a><a href={"#pn-customized-writing-packages-1u8zhca"}>{"Packages"}</a><a href={"#pn-customized-writing-guarantee-vy6yyz"}>{"Guarantee"}</a><a href={"#pn-customized-writing-client-stories-6o8lri"}>{"Client stories"}</a><a href={"#pn-customized-writing-faq-1shkspl"}>{"FAQ"}</a></div></nav><section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-customized-writing-who-we-serve-1vyhfoc"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Who we serve"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Who commissions bespoke writing."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Six kinds of client, and one shared situation: a document that has to exist, no obvious person to write it, and a date."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"auds rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "0" }}><b>{"Clinicians in practice"}</b><span>{"A talk, a report, a letter, a leaflet — the writing that accumulates around a clinical job and never appears in anybody’s objectives. Usually one document at a time, usually against a date."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "1" }}><b>{"Physician-researchers"}</b><span>{"The documents that surround a study without being the paper: the rebuttal, the conference talk, the departmental report, the publication plan for what the dataset will support over the next two years."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "2" }}><b>{"Medical academics and faculty"}</b><span>{"Teaching material, curriculum content, committee papers and the writing that a promotion case rests on, where the audience is a panel rather than a reviewer."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "3" }}><b>{"Postgraduates and specialty trainees"}</b><span>{"Inside the boundaries set out above: editing where the institution permits it, statistical collaboration, converting an examined thesis chapter into a paper, and coaching on how to write the next one yourself."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "4" }}><b>{"Key opinion leaders and speakers"}</b><span>{"Talks, slide decks, commentary and interview preparation, where declaring who wrote what matters more than usual because the audience is watching for it."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "5" }}><b>{"Hospitals, societies and industry teams"}</b><span>{"Document sets rather than documents, where the real requirement is consistency across all of them and a house style settled once. Under GPP 2022 where the underlying research is company-sponsored."}</span></div> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", borderTop: "0", marginTop: "0" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Why a document set is cheaper than the documents in it"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"Because the expensive part is not the writing. It is establishing the facts: finding the figure, checking it against its source, resolving the two places it is reported differently, and deciding which version is right. Do that once for a study and you can then write the paper, the abstract, the poster, the talk, the departmental report and the patient explainer from one verified set — and they will agree with each other, which they otherwise reliably do not. Commissioned separately over eighteen months by three different people, the same work is done three times and produces three documents that disagree in small ways nobody notices until somebody does. Where we can see a set coming, we will say so and quote for it, even when you asked for one document."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-customized-writing-how-it-works-18syixm"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"How it works"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Six stages, and the first one is about the reader."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Register is settled before length, and length before structure. Getting that order wrong is how a document ends up thorough and useless."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"steps6"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "0" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage one"}</span> <h3>{"The reader, and what they do next"}</h3> <p><b>{"Before anything is quoted."}</b>{" Who reads this, in what setting, with how much time, and what decision they make afterwards. That settles the register, the length and the structure in a single conversation, and it occasionally settles that the document you asked for is not the document that will work."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "1" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage two"}</span> <h3>{"Authorship and attribution, settled in writing"}</h3> <p><b>{"Who is an author, who is acknowledged, and what the declaration will say."}</b>{" Checked against the four ICMJE criteria where the document is a publication, and against the house or society convention where it is not. Our own contribution is settled here too, in writing, with the acknowledgement wording agreed before drafting rather than negotiated after."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "2" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage three"}</span> <h3>{"The writer, matched to the field"}</h3> <p><b>{"By clinical or scientific field rather than by availability."}</b>{" For a document set, one writer across all of it so the facts do not drift between documents — a figure given as 88.7% in one and 89% in another is a discrepancy rather than a rounding choice, and it is exactly what a careful reader notices first."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "3" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage four"}</span> <h3>{"Drafting, against the sources"}</h3> <p><b>{"Every factual claim traced to a source you can open."}</b>{" Not a citation matched to a sentence, but the cited work read against the statement it supports — which is a different and slower thing, and which is where errors that have propagated through a literature for years get caught."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "4" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage five"}</span> <h3>{"Read by somebody who did not write it"}</h3> <p><b>{"Against the brief, not against the draft."}</b>{" Does this document do what stage one said it had to do, for the reader stage one identified? Plus the mechanical checks: originality and AI screening with every match classified rather than a percentage handed over, numerical consistency across a document set, and references verified against their sources."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "5" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage six"}</span> <h3>{"Your revisions, and the declaration"}</h3> <p><b>{"Revised until it is right, inside the scope agreed."}</b>{" Delivered with the acknowledgement wording, the written permission for it, the funding sentence where the work was paid for, and the AI disclosure where any was used — all three in the form the ICMJE’s January 2026 guidance asks for, ready to paste."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Where AI is used, and where it is not"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The register is the work."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Bespoke writing succeeds or fails on whether it sounds like the person whose name is on it and lands with the audience it was written for. That is the part generated text is worst at, and the part clients notice first."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps caps--3 rv rv-d1"} style={{ marginTop: "0" }}> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What we use it for"}</b><span>{"Research and source-gathering. Checking claims against what is cited. Consistency of terminology across a set of documents. Reformatting to a template."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What we do not use it for"}</b><span>{"Writing in a named person’s voice without their input; clinical or scientific claims not verified against source; and anything published under an author who has not read and agreed it."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What goes in your declaration"}</b><span>{"The tool, the stage it was used at, and the human oversight applied — because journals, funders and the ICMJE January 2026 update all now expect it, and an undeclared tool found later is treated as a research integrity matter rather than a style preference."}</span></div> <div className={"caps__note"}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Why we publish no accuracy figure of our own"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"These tools are marketed with precision and recall figures, and the honest problem is who measured them. In June 2026 a Cochrane journal retracted a validation study of one widely sold tool because every author held equity in the product, and the conflict had not been caught in review."}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"So Pubrica quotes no self-generated accuracy number, because ours would carry exactly the same conflict. What we will do is tell you which tool was used on your project, at which stage, and show you what a human changed after it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section section--tight"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap band band--split rv"}> <div> <h2>{"Tell us the document and the reader. That is most of the brief."}</h2> <p className={"lede"} style={{ marginTop: "18px" }}>{"Two business days, at no cost: what register it needs, how long it should be, what it will take, and whether the thing you are asking for is the thing that will work. Occasionally the answer is that a fifteen-minute talk is a better use of the material than the paper you asked for."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions"} style={{ marginTop: "28px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/pricing/"} data-nav={""}>{"All pricing"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"jcard"}> <div className={"jcard__bar"}>{"What you provide"}</div> <div className={"jcard__body"}> <div className={"jcard__grid"}> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The document"}</b><span>{"What it is, and what it is for"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The reader"}</b><span>{"Who reads it, and what they decide afterwards"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The length"}</b><span>{"A limit if there is one, an estimate if not"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The material"}</b><span>{"Data, slides, notes, a previous version"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The rules"}</b><span>{"House style, template, or the body’s own format"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The date"}</b><span>{"The real one"}</span></div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note"}>{"The second line is the one that changes the document most and the one clients most often skip. “A report on our service’s outcomes” could be a board paper asking for two posts, a paper for a journal, a poster for a society meeting or a handout for referrers — four documents with almost nothing in common except the numbers in them. Telling us what the reader does after reading it settles the register, the length and the structure in one sentence."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"The question this page has to answer first"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"If somebody else writes it, whose work is it?"}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"A page selling writing to physicians cannot put “no ghostwriting” in a bullet list and move on, and you will see plenty that do — sometimes in a sentence whose missing conjunction makes it read as an admission. So here is the actual position, with the instrument that decides it. Run any contributor through the four ICMJE criteria and the tool below tells you whether they are an author or an acknowledgement, and gives you the wording."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"tgrid"} data-tls={""} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <div className={"tk rv"} id={"cw-auth"} data-tool={"aut"} data-open={"1"}> <div className={"tk__h"}> <p className={"tk__n"}>{"01"}</p> <div> <h3 className={"tk__t"}><button type={"button"} aria-expanded={"true"} aria-controls={"cw-auth-body"}>{"ICMJE authorship qualifier"}</button></h3> <p className={"tk__s"}>{"One contributor at a time against the four criteria, with the acknowledgement, funding and AI wording produced ready to paste."}</p> <span className={"tk__tag"}>{"Runs in your browser · nothing sent anywhere"}</span> </div> <span className={"tk__x"} aria-hidden={"true"} /> </div> <div className={"tk__body"} id={"cw-auth-body"}> <div className={"tfm"}> <div className={"tf tf--wide"}><span id={"lbl-cw-role"}>{"Who is this person?"}</span><div className={"tseg"} data-seg={"role"} role={"group"} aria-labelledby={"lbl-cw-role"}><button type={"button"} data-v={"inv"} aria-pressed={"true"}>{"An investigator"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"data"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Collected the data"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"stat"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"The statistician"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"sup"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Supervisor or head of department"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"wrt"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"A professional writer"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"spon"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"A sponsor’s employee"}</button></div></div> <label className={"tf"}><span>{"Their name, for the wording"}</span><em>{"Optional. Stays in your browser; nothing is sent anywhere."}</em><input type={"text"} data-k={"name"} placeholder={"e.g. Dr A. Sharma"} /></label> <label className={"tf"}><span>{"Who funded the assistance"}</span><em>{"Optional. Only used in the funding sentence."}</em><input type={"text"} data-k={"spon"} placeholder={"e.g. the authors, or a named sponsor"} /></label> <div className={"tchk tf--wide"}> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"conc"} checked={true} /><span><b>{"Criterion 1a."}</b>{" Conceived the question, or designed the study"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"acq"} /><span><b>{"Criterion 1b."}</b>{" Acquired the data"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"an"} /><span><b>{"Criterion 1c."}</b>{" Analysed or interpreted the data"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"draft"} /><span><b>{"Criterion 2a."}</b>{" Drafted the work"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"rev"} checked={true} /><span><b>{"Criterion 2b."}</b>{" Revised it critically for important intellectual content — not simply read and approved it"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"appr"} checked={true} /><span><b>{"Criterion 3."}</b>{" Will give final approval of the version to be published"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"acct"} checked={true} /><span><b>{"Criterion 4."}</b>{" Agrees to be accountable for all aspects of the work, including investigating questions about any part of it"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"paid"} /><span>{"The contribution was paid for"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"ai"} /><span>{"Generative AI was used somewhere in preparing the work"}</span></label> </div> </div> <div className={"tout"} data-out={""}><div className={"tout__hd"}><b>{"Qualifies for authorship"}</b><span>{"4 of 4 criteria met"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--has"}><b>{"1 · Substantial contribution — met"}</b><span>{"To the conception or design of the work, "}<i>{"or"}</i>{" to the acquisition, analysis or interpretation of data. Any one of those three satisfies it; the \"or\" is in the ICMJE wording and is routinely misread as an \"and\"."}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--has"}><b>{"2 · Drafting or critical revision — met"}</b><span>{"Drafting the work, or reviewing it critically for important intellectual content. Reading a draft and agreeing with it does not meet this, which is the criterion honorary authors most often fail."}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--has"}><b>{"3 · Final approval — met"}</b><span>{"Of the version to be published. The easiest to satisfy and the easiest to forget to record."}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--has"}><b>{"4 · Accountability — met"}</b><span>{"Agreement to be accountable for all aspects of the work, including ensuring that questions about the accuracy or integrity of "}<i>{"any part"}</i>{" of it are appropriately investigated and resolved. This is an undertaking about the whole paper, not about your section."}</span></div><div className={"tverd"}><p><b>{"Qualifies for authorship."}</b>{" All four criteria are met. Note that meeting them is not optional in the other direction either: the ICMJE states that everybody designated as an author should meet all four, and that everybody who meets all four should be identified as an author. Somebody who has met them and is being left off is as much a problem as somebody who has not and is being included."}</p><p><b>{"The investigator."}</b>{" Usually meets all four without difficulty. The one to check is criterion 2: on multi-site studies a site investigator who recruited patients and never saw a draft has met criterion 1 and not criterion 2, and the fix is to send them the draft rather than to quietly include them."}</p></div><p className={"tsub"}>{"The wording, ready to paste"}</p><pre className={"tcode"} data-copytext={""}>{"CRediT-style contribution statement, for the authors’ section:\n\n[contributor name] contributed to the conception and design of the study; revised the work critically for important intellectual content; approved the final version to be published; and agrees to be accountable for all aspects of the work."}</pre><button type={"button"} className={"tcopy"} data-copy={""}>{"Copy the wording"}</button><p className={"tmeth"}><b>{"Source, and what this is not."}</b>{" The four criteria and the treatment of non-author contributors are from the ICMJE Recommendations, updated January 2026 — note that the browsable pages on the ICMJE site still carry older text in places, so the PDF is the authoritative version. The ICMJE lists writing assistance, technical editing, language editing and proofreading among the activities that alone do not qualify a contributor for authorship, says such contributors should be acknowledged with their contribution described, and advises editors to require the corresponding author to obtain written permission from everybody acknowledged. It also requires disclosure of the sponsor’s role including in the writing of the report. The phrase “medical writer” does not appear anywhere in the Recommendations, and neither does “ghost”; the term used is writing assistance. "}<b>{"This is a working aid, not an adjudication."}</b>{" Your target journal’s own authorship policy governs, several journals add requirements the ICMJE does not, and the corresponding author decides."}</p></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d1"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", marginTop: "26px" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"What we will not claim here, and why we are saying so"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"“Ethical content development, no ghost writing, data manipulation” is a real bullet from a real page in this market. The missing conjunction turns a list of things a supplier does not do into a claim that they do the last one, and on a page about research integrity that is not a typographical matter. It generally sits beside an offer to write theses and dissertations and a claim of adherence to the ICMJE and ISMPP, which is a contradiction rather than an oversight: a professional writer’s contribution must be acknowledged under the ICMJE, and a thesis written for submission as a student’s own work cannot be acknowledged at all without defeating the purpose. The same pages tend to assert ISO 27001 and ISO 9001:2015 certification with no registrar, scope or certificate number. Here is ours: we hold ISO 9001:2015 under certificate H3CR9TCU20251212INDQM10N and we quote the number every time. We make no ISO 27001 claim on this page, because we will not assert a certification without a number beside it. Ask any supplier for theirs."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-customized-writing-our-experts-1aaq5aj"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Our experts"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The people who will actually do the work."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Not a pool you are allocated from. The same named team stays with your project from scoping to delivery, the handover says which of them did which stage, and your project coordinator introduces them by name before anything starts."}</p> </div> </div>  <div className={"revw"}> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"SME"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Subject expert"}</b><span>{"A subject matter expert assigned from your topic, not from a rota"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Decides what the work is allowed to claim. Matched to your topic rather than allocated from a rota, and the one who tells you plainly when the evidence will not carry the conclusion you were hoping for."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Question, scope, interpretation"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"ICMJE, COPE, PRISMA"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Field"}</span><b>{"Matched to your topic"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"DD"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Dr. Divya"}</b><span>{"PhD in Life Science · second reviewer"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Reads independently of the first pass and reconciles, because most errors in this work are transcription errors rather than reasoning ones. Disagreements are logged and adjudicated, never quietly resolved."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Independent second read"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"RoB 2, ROBINS-I, QUADAS-3, JBI"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Adjudicated by"}</span><b>{"A third reviewer"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"DA"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Dr. Antony"}</b><span>{"Information specialist"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Finds what the work is built on. Writes the search line by line for each platform and hands it over dated and reproducible, so a reviewer, an editor or an assessor can run it again."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Search and retrieval"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"PRISMA-S, PRESS"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Second-checked by"}</span><b>{"A second information specialist"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"MJ"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Mr. John"}</b><span>{"M.Sc. in Statistics · statistician"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Owns anything the numbers decide. Says before the analysis exists whether the data can answer the question, and hands over the code so the whole thing can be re-run without us."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Analysis and certainty"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"GRADE, SWiM, CONSORT"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Tools"}</span><b>{"R, Stata, SAS, RevMan"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-customized-writing-sample-work-ytogif"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Sample work"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"One finding, four documents, four different sentences."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"This is the whole argument of this page in one exhibit: the same result from the same study, written for a journal, for a board, for a referring colleague and for a patient. Nothing is dumbed down and nothing is dressed up. What changes is what the reader needs in order to do the thing they will do next. Use the tabs, then open the full sample below."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"sample"}> <div className={"doc rv"}> <p className={"doc__k"}>{"Register comparison"}</p> <h3 className={"doc__h"}>{"One result · four readers · four documents"}</h3> <p className={"doc__sub"}>{"The journal · the board · the colleague · the patient"}</p> <div className={"doc__tabs"} role={"tablist"} aria-label={"Four registers"}> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"cw-t1"} aria-controls={"cw-p1"} aria-selected={"true"} tabIndex={0}><i>{"1"}</i>{"Journal"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"cw-t2"} aria-controls={"cw-p2"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"2"}</i>{"Board"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"cw-t3"} aria-controls={"cw-p3"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"3"}</i>{"Colleague"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"cw-t4"} aria-controls={"cw-p4"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"4"}</i>{"Patient"}</button> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"cw-p1"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"cw-t1"}> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Reader"}</dt><dd>{"A reviewer and, later, a researcher deciding whether to build on this."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"What they need"}</dt><dd>{"Enough method to judge whether the finding is believable, and a claim proportionate to the design."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"The sentence"}</dt><dd>{"“Introduction of the pathway was associated with a shorter median time to treatment (4.1 h, IQR 2.8–6.0, vs 6.7 h, IQR 4.2–9.9; p<0.001). The comparison is uncontrolled and staffing changed over the same period; these findings support prospective evaluation.”"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"What is doing the work"}</dt><dd>{"“Associated with” rather than “reduced”, the interquartile ranges, and the sentence acknowledging the confounding before a reviewer raises it."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Length"}</dt><dd>{"Two sentences inside a 3,500-word paper."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Fails if"}</dt><dd>{"It claims causation, or omits the staffing change that a reviewer will find in the methods anyway."}</dd></dl> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"cw-p2"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"cw-t2"} hidden={true}> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Reader"}</dt><dd>{"A committee reading twelve papers in an evening, deciding whether to fund two posts."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"What they need"}</dt><dd>{"The ask, the number behind it, and the risk of not doing it. In that order, on the first page."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"The sentence"}</dt><dd>{"“Median time to treatment fell from 6.7 to 4.1 hours after the pathway was introduced. Sustaining it requires two additional posts from April; without them the rota cannot cover the evening period in which most of the delay occurred.”"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"What is doing the work"}</dt><dd>{"The ask in the second sentence rather than on page four, and the consequence stated as an operational fact rather than a warning."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Length"}</dt><dd>{"Two pages, with the recommendation in the first paragraph."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Fails if"}</dt><dd>{"It opens with methodology. A committee that has not found the ask by paragraph two defers the paper."}</dd></dl> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"cw-p3"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"cw-t3"} hidden={true}> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Reader"}</dt><dd>{"A referring GP or a colleague in another specialty, reading between patients."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"What they need"}</dt><dd>{"What changed for them: who to refer, how, and what happens differently now."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"The sentence"}</dt><dd>{"“Patients referred through the new pathway are now seen and treated in about four hours rather than about seven. Refer directly on the number below rather than through the general line; you do not need to call first.”"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"What is doing the work"}</dt><dd>{"The instruction. A colleague does not need the interquartile range; they need to know that the old habit is now the slow route."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Length"}</dt><dd>{"One side of A4, or six lines in a newsletter."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Fails if"}</dt><dd>{"It reads as a research summary. Colleagues skim these; the action has to survive being skimmed."}</dd></dl> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"cw-p4"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"cw-t4"} hidden={true}> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Reader"}</dt><dd>{"A patient or a relative, often anxious, often reading on a phone in a waiting area."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"What they need"}</dt><dd>{"What will happen to them, in what order, and roughly when."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"The sentence"}</dt><dd>{"“We have changed how we work so that treatment starts sooner. Most people now start treatment within about four hours of arriving. A nurse will explain each step as it happens.”"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"What is doing the work"}</dt><dd>{"“Most people” rather than a median, and the last sentence, which answers the question the leaflet was not asked: what do I do now."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Reading level"}</dt><dd>{"Grade 6 as measured by SMOG. Measured, not asserted — see our "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"#/patient-education-content"} data-nav={""}>{"patient education page"}</a>{" for the instruments and the target."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Fails if"}</dt><dd>{"It gives a median with an interquartile range, which is accurate and unreadable, or promises four hours, which is a median presented as a guarantee."}</dd></dl> </div> <p className={"doc__foot"}><span>{"One verified fact set · four documents"}</span><span>{"Written once, checked once"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"prose"}> <p>{"Four documents from one result, and only one number appears in all four. "}<b>{"Use the tabs to see each."}</b></p> <p><b>{"Nothing here is simplification."}</b>{" The patient version is not the journal version with the statistics removed; it answers a different question, because the patient is deciding whether to be reassured and the reviewer is deciding whether to believe the method. Writing one and cutting it down produces a document that serves neither."}</p> <p><b>{"The expensive part is the fact set, not the writing."}</b>{" Establishing that the medians are 6.7 and 4.1, that both are defensible, and that the staffing change happened in the same period takes longer than writing any one of these. Done once, it produces four documents that agree with each other — which is not the usual outcome when they are commissioned separately eighteen months apart."}</p> </div> <div className={"factors"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Register settled before length"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"From who reads it and what they do next."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"One verified fact set behind all of them"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"So the documents cannot drift apart."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Claims proportionate in every version"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"Including the patient one, where a median is not a promise."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Reading level measured where it matters"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"With the instrument and the target both recorded."}</span></span></div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}>{"Ask for the sample work and you get a register comparison built round a finding of yours — the same result written for the readers you actually have."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions"} style={{ marginTop: "16px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"#fsm-cw"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-cw"}>{"Read the full comparison"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/insights/sample-work/"}>{"Discover more"}</a> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"fsm rv rv-d2"} data-fsm={""}> <button type={"button"} className={"fsm__t"} data-fsm-t={""} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"fsm-cw"}> <span><b>{"Read the full register comparison"}</b><em>{"The whole deliverable, on this page — the fact set, all four documents in full, and the declarations attached to each"}</em></span> <i aria-hidden={"true"} /> </button> <div className={"fsm__p"} id={"fsm-cw"}> <div className={"fsm__doc"}> <p className={"fsm__k"}>{"Customized writing · sample register comparison"}</p> <h3 className={"fsm__hd"}>{"One service evaluation, four documents"}</h3> <p className={"fsm__sub"}>{"A composite built from real work. The service, the institution, the condition and the figures have all been changed; the structure, the register differences and the declarations are as delivered. Ask us and we will send one built around a finding of yours."}</p> <h4><span>{"1"}</span>{"The fact set, established once"}</h4> <p>{"Before any of the four documents existed, one verified fact set was built and signed off. This is the expensive part and the part that is invisible in every finished document."}</p> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Fact"}</th><th>{"Value"}</th><th>{"How it was verified"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Median time to treatment, before"}</td><td>{"6.7 h (IQR 4.2–9.9)"}</td><td>{"Recomputed from the raw extract rather than taken from the earlier audit summary, which had used a mean and a different denominator."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Median time to treatment, after"}</td><td>{"4.1 h (IQR 2.8–6.0)"}</td><td>{"Same extract, same definition of the clock start — which had to be settled first, because two teams were measuring from different events."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Patients, before and after"}</td><td>{"318 and 274"}</td><td>{"With exclusions listed. Eleven records were excluded for incomplete timing and that is stated rather than absorbed."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Period"}</td><td>{"18 months either side"}</td><td>{"Stated in both documents that make a comparison."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"The confounder"}</td><td>{"Evening staffing increased in month four of the \"after\" period"}</td><td>{"Found while checking, not while writing. It changes what the journal version may claim and it belongs in the board paper as a risk."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"The ask"}</td><td>{"2.0 WTE from April"}</td><td>{"Costed with the finance team, because a board paper with an uncosted ask is returned."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"The confounder is the point of doing this once. Found at the fact-checking stage it shaped all four documents honestly. Found by a reviewer eight months later it would have cost the paper, and found by a board member it would have cost the posts."}</p> <h4><span>{"2"}</span>{"The journal version"}</h4> <p><b>{"Reader:"}</b>{" a peer reviewer, then researchers deciding whether to build on it. "}<b>{"Length:"}</b>{" two sentences in the results and three in the discussion of a 3,500-word paper. "}<b>{"Governs:"}</b>{" SQUIRE 2.0, as a quality improvement report."}</p> <p><i>{"“Median time from arrival to treatment was 6.7 hours (IQR 4.2–9.9) in the 18 months before the pathway was introduced (n=318) and 4.1 hours (IQR 2.8–6.0) in the 18 months after (n=274; p<0.001). Eleven records were excluded for incomplete timing data.”"}</i></p> <p><i>{"“This comparison is uncontrolled. Evening nursing establishment increased in the fourth month of the post-implementation period, and the majority of the observed delay in the earlier period occurred in the evening; the two changes cannot be separated in these data. These findings support prospective evaluation of the pathway rather than its adoption elsewhere on this evidence.”"}</i></p> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"The second paragraph is the one the author did not want and the one that makes the first believable. A reviewer who finds an unmentioned co-intervention treats everything else in the paper differently; a reviewer who is told about it in the discussion reads the rest more generously."}</p> <h4><span>{"3"}</span>{"The board paper"}</h4> <p><b>{"Reader:"}</b>{" a committee reading twelve papers in an evening. "}<b>{"Length:"}</b>{" two pages, recommendation first. "}<b>{"Governs:"}</b>{" the trust’s own board paper template."}</p> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Section"}</th><th>{"Content"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Recommendation"}</td><td>{"“The Board is asked to approve 2.0 WTE band 6 posts from 1 April, at a full-year cost of [x].” First line, not page four."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Why"}</td><td>{"“Median time to treatment fell from 6.7 to 4.1 hours following introduction of the pathway. Most of the improvement was in the evening period.”"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"The honest caveat"}</td><td>{"“Evening nursing establishment also increased during this period. The improvement cannot be attributed to the pathway alone, and the posts are required to sustain either explanation.” This strengthens the ask rather than weakening it, because both readings need the staff."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Risk of not approving"}</td><td>{"Stated as an operational consequence with a date, not as a warning."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"What happens next"}</td><td>{"Reporting back at six months, with the measure named in advance."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <h4><span>{"4"}</span>{"The note to referrers"}</h4> <p><b>{"Reader:"}</b>{" a GP or a colleague in another specialty, reading between patients. "}<b>{"Length:"}</b>{" one side, or six lines in a newsletter. "}<b>{"Governs:"}</b>{" nothing formal, which is why it is so often written badly."}</p> <p><i>{"“Patients referred through the new pathway are now seen and treated in about four hours, rather than about seven. Refer directly on [number] — you no longer need to call the general line first, and referrals made that way are slower. The service runs seven days, 08:00 to 22:00. Outside those hours, refer as before.”"}</i></p> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"Four sentences, three of which are instructions. No interquartile range, no p-value and no mention of the staffing change, because none of those alters what the reader does. What does alter it is the second sentence: the old habit is now the slow route, and saying so plainly is the entire purpose of the document."}</p> <h4><span>{"5"}</span>{"The patient leaflet"}</h4> <p><b>{"Reader:"}</b>{" a patient or relative, often anxious, often on a phone. "}<b>{"Length:"}</b>{" under 300 words. "}<b>{"Measured at:"}</b>{" grade 6 by SMOG, against the target agreed with the clinical team."}</p> <p><i>{"“We have changed how we work so that treatment starts sooner."}</i></p> <p><i>{"Most people now start treatment within about four hours of arriving. Some wait longer, usually because we need more test results first."}</i></p> <p><i>{"A nurse will tell you what is happening at each step. You can ask them at any time how long the next step is likely to take."}</i></p> <p><i>{"If you are waiting and you feel worse, tell any member of staff straight away. Do not wait to be asked.”"}</i></p> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"Three things are deliberate here. “Most people” rather than a median, because a median presented to a patient reads as a promise. The second sentence of the second paragraph, because a leaflet that only describes the good case makes the bad case feel like a failure. And the last paragraph, which is the safety line and the reason the leaflet is worth writing at all."}</p> <h4><span>{"6"}</span>{"Declarations, on each document"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Document"}</th><th>{"What it carries"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Journal paper"}</td><td>{"Authorship assessed against all four ICMJE criteria, with two contributors moved between author and acknowledgement as a result. Writing assistance acknowledged, with written permission obtained and the funding of that assistance stated. AI disclosure per ICMJE section V where any was used."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Board paper"}</td><td>{"Author and sponsoring director named per the trust’s template, with the writing support noted in the version history rather than in it."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Referrer note"}</td><td>{"The clinical lead named as the contact, because a note without a named human to ring is ignored."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Patient leaflet"}</td><td>{"Review date, version number, and the reading level with the instrument used to measure it — so the next person to revise it knows what target to hold."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"The acknowledgement is the point. Declared writing assistance is legitimate and undeclared authorship is not, and the difference between the two is one sentence that costs nothing. Any document we write that could not carry that sentence is a document we would have declined."}</p> <div className={"fsm__foot"}> <p>{"Prepared by Pubrica. Pubrica is a trading name of Guires"}<sup className={"reg"}>{"®"}</sup>{", registered in England, Wales and India."}</p> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/downloads/pubrica-customized-writing-sample.pdf"} download={""}>{"Download this as a PDF"}</a> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-customized-writing-packages-1u8zhca"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Packages"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Three tiers, and a set price for a set."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Priced on length, register and how much fact-checking the material needs. Every figure is a floor with its cap beside it, because a word count is the only honest way to make “from” mean anything on a page this broad."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"tiers rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Essential"}</span> <h3>{"One short document"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Individual clinicians with a single piece to write and a date — a letter, a note to referrers, a short report, a rebuttal"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $180"}</b><span>{"up to 1,200 words · 1 register · 1 revision"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"4–7 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"The register settled from the reader before anything is drafted"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Written by somebody qualified in your clinical field"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Every factual claim traced to a source you can open"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Originality and AI screening, with matches classified rather than counted"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"The acknowledgement wording and the written permission for it"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Add later: a second register of the same material; design and layout."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-cw"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-cw"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Essential"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier tier--pick"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Professional"}</span> <h3>{"One substantial document"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Physician-researchers and faculty writing something that has to stand up: a white paper, a CME module, a position statement, a committee paper"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $560"}</b><span>{"up to 3,500 words · 20 references · 1 revision round"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"8–12 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Everything in Essential"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Literature support, with each cited work read against the claim it carries"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Structured to the body’s own template where there is one"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Authorship checked against the four ICMJE criteria and agreed in writing"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Read by a second person against the brief, not against the draft"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Tables, figures and a reference library in your preferred manager"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Add later: further registers; slide deck; translation."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-cw"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-cw"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Professional"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Advanced"}</span> <h3>{"A long document, or a set"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Senior clinicians, departments and institutional clients with a set of documents that have to agree with each other"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $1,080"}</b><span>{"up to 6,000 words, or 4 documents from one fact set"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"12–18 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Everything in Professional"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"One verified fact set behind every document, so they cannot drift"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Numerical consistency checked across the whole set, including rounding"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"One writer across all of it, with a house style settled once"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Visuals: tables, charts, a graphical summary or a slide deck"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Two revision rounds, and reviewer or committee comments handled"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Larger sets, ongoing retainers and publication plans are quoted on scope."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-cw"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-cw"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Advanced"}</a> </div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "22px" }}>{"Additions are quoted alongside any tier: a second or third register of the same material, which is far cheaper than commissioning it separately; design and layout for print or screen; a slide deck and speaker notes built from the document; translation and localisation by a subject-matter translator; a visual abstract or infographic; and rapid delivery where capacity allows, quoted on capacity rather than on urgency."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "24px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/pricing/"} data-nav={""}>{"All pricing"}</a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-customized-writing-guarantee-vy6yyz"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Guaranteed quality"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What we promise, and what we will not."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"A page this broad needs its boundaries stated rather than implied. Here are the terms before you commit to anything."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"gtee rv"}> <div className={"gtee__top"}> <p className={"gtee__k"}>{"The Pubrica guarantee"}</p> <h3 className={"gtee__h"}>{"We keep working until it is right."}</h3> <p className={"gtee__p"}>{"Revision until the document does what the brief said it had to do, for the reader the brief identified, with no cap on rounds inside the scope agreed."}</p> </div> <div className={"gtee__grid"}> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"01"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Judged against the brief"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"Not against the draft. The question at review is whether this document works for the reader we identified in stage one, which is a harder test than whether it reads well."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"02"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Our error, our cost"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"A fact wrong, a reference that does not support the sentence it is attached to, a figure inconsistent across a document set — if it came from us, correcting it is free and you hear about it from us first."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"03"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Delivered on the date agreed"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"Committee dates, conference deadlines and print runs do not move. If a date is genuinely at risk you hear it early with what can be done."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"04"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Your document stays yours"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"We draft, argue a view and tell you plainly when we disagree with a claim. What goes out in your name is settled by you, every time."}</p></div> </div> <p className={"gtee__foot"}><b>{"The limits, stated plainly."}</b>{" We do not write theses, dissertations or any other assessed work for submission as a student’s own — providing, arranging or advertising that is a criminal offence in England under the Skills and Post-16 Education Act 2022 and an offence in Australia under the amended TEQSA Act, and university regulations prohibit it everywhere we work. We do not offer a “guaranteed plagiarism-free” output, because no supplier can guarantee an absolute; what we provide is an iThenticate report with every match read and classified, which is more useful and is actually true. We do not write to a predetermined conclusion, omit an inconvenient finding, or describe an association in the grammar of causation. We do not write anything that would have to conceal who wrote it. And we do not claim certifications without a number: we hold ISO 9001:2015 under certificate H3CR9TCU20251212INDQM10N, and where we make no claim on this page it is because we are not making one."}</p> </div> <div style={{ height: "clamp(26px,3vw,38px)" }} /> <div className={"pledges rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"The brief conversation is free"}</p> <p>{"What register the document needs, how long it should be, what it will take, and whether the thing you have asked for is the thing that will work. Two business days, no cost, no obligation. It quite often ends with a different document from the one in the enquiry — a talk instead of a paper, four short pieces instead of one long one — and that is the conversation doing its job."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"Declared, not ghosted"}</p> <p>{"The ICMJE lists writing assistance among the activities that do not on their own qualify somebody for authorship, says such contributors should be acknowledged with their contribution described, and advises editors to require written permission from everybody acknowledged. So a Pubrica writer is named in the acknowledgements, we supply the wording and the permission, and you keep authorship. Where a contribution genuinely meets all four criteria we say so and let you decide; nothing bars a writer from being an author, and it is the contribution that decides rather than the invoice."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"AI, declared to you first"}</p> <p>{"Any use of generative AI in preparing your document is declared to you before it is declared anywhere else, and handled to the ICMJE’s January 2026 guidance: never as an author, disclosed in the acknowledgements where it assisted with writing, and described in the methods with the tool, the version and the prompts where it touched data or figures. AI-generated material is not cited as a primary source, and output is checked rather than trusted — the failure mode is authoritative-sounding text that is wrong, and it is our job to catch it rather than yours."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"Confidentiality and data handling"}</p> <p>{"A non-disclosure agreement is signed before any material moves, and writers and project staff are bound by internal confidentiality agreements as well. Unpublished material, commercial information and draft documents are held under the UK GDPR on access-controlled systems within a quality management system certified to ISO 9001:2015, kept only as long as the project needs them, never used to train anything and never shared outside your project team. Where a document contains patient identifiers we ask you to remove them before sending rather than removing them ourselves."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-customized-writing-client-stories-6o8lri"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"In their words"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Three documents, and what changed."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Rephrased from client feedback. Each quote is a placeholder until the named client has confirmed it in writing."}</p> </div> </div>  <div className={"tcar rv"}> <div className={"tcar__track"} data-tcar={""} tabIndex={0} role={"group"} aria-label={"Client testimonials, scrollable"}> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“I asked for a paper. They asked who was going to read it and why, and what I actually needed was a two-page board paper.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}><span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--c"}><span className={"mcov__k"}>{"SERVICE"}<br />{"EVALUATION"}</span><span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Board"}<br />{"Paper"}</span><span className={"mcov__r"} /></span></span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Name to be confirmed"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Clinical lead · region to be confirmed"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Delivered as"}</b><span>{"Board paper and referrer note"}</span><i>{"—"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“They told me they would not write my thesis and explained why in two sentences. Then they told me what they could do, which was more useful.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}><span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--e"}><span className={"mcov__k"}>{"POSTGRADUATE"}<br />{"RESEARCH"}</span><span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Statistical"}<br />{"Collaboration"}</span><span className={"mcov__r"} /></span></span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Name to be confirmed"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Specialty trainee · region to be confirmed"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Delivered as"}</b><span>{"Analysis and named collaboration"}</span><i>{"—"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“Our head of department was on the author list of every paper the unit produced. The criteria conversation was overdue and somebody external had to start it.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}><span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--b"}><span className={"mcov__k"}>{"RESEARCH"}<br />{"UNIT"}</span><span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Authorship"}<br />{"Policy"}</span><span className={"mcov__r"} /></span></span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Name to be confirmed"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Research manager · region to be confirmed"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Delivered as"}</b><span>{"House authorship policy"}</span><i>{"—"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> </div> <div className={"tcar__foot"}> <a className={"btn btn--ghost tcar__more"} href={"/testimonial/"}>{"Explore more client testimonials"}</a> <div className={"tcar__dots"} data-tdots={""} aria-hidden={"true"} style={{ display: "none" }} /> <div className={"tcar__btns"} style={{ display: "none" }}> <button type={"button"} className={"tcar__btn"} data-tprev={""} aria-label={"Previous testimonial"} disabled={true}><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M9 5l7 7-7 7"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.6"} strokeLinecap={"round"} strokeLinejoin={"round"} /></svg></button> <button type={"button"} className={"tcar__btn"} data-tnext={""} aria-label={"More testimonials"} disabled={true}><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M9 5l7 7-7 7"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.6"} strokeLinecap={"round"} strokeLinejoin={"round"} /></svg></button> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-customized-writing-faq-1shkspl"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"} style={{ display: "block" }}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Customized writing FAQs"}</p> <h2>{"Eight questions clients ask."}</h2> <p className={"prose"} style={{ marginTop: "20px" }}>{"Not sure what register your document needs, or where the line is on academic work? "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Ask an expert"}</a>{" — no quote required."}</p> </div> <div className={"faq__list rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"cw-0"}><span>{"What is customized medical writing, and how does it work?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"cw-0"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"It is writing for the documents that do not have a service page of their own: a departmental report, a CME module, a conference talk, a rebuttal letter, a white paper, a note to referrers, a medico-legal report. The process starts with the reader rather than with the subject. Who reads this, in what setting, with how much time, and what do they do afterwards — those four answers settle the register, the length and the structure before anything is drafted, and they are the reason the same clinical fact becomes four genuinely different sentences depending on where it lands. From there a writer qualified in your field drafts it, every factual claim is traced to a source that can be opened, a second person reads it against the brief rather than against the draft, and it comes back with the acknowledgement wording and the written permission for it attached."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"cw-1"}><span>{"Will you write my thesis or dissertation?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"cw-1"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"No. We do not write theses, dissertations or any other assessed work to be submitted as a student’s own. In England, providing, arranging or advertising such a service is a criminal offence under sections 27 and 28 of the Skills and Post-16 Education Act 2022. In Australia, providing or advertising academic cheating services is an offence under the TEQSA Act as amended in 2020, carrying penalties of up to 500 penalty units and two years’ imprisonment. The QAA defines contract cheating as a third party completing work that a student submits as their own where that input is not permitted, and university regulations prohibit it and typically allow only limited, declared editing and proofreading. What we do instead sits inside those boundaries: language editing to the extent your institution permits and declared where it requires declaration; statistical analysis and interpretation as a named collaborator; converting an already-examined chapter into a journal article, which is publication rather than assessment; and coaching on writing it yourself. Ask your supervisor or research office where your institution draws the line before you ask us, and we will ask you what they said."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"cw-2"}><span>{"Is using a medical writer ghostwriting?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"cw-2"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Only if it is concealed, and the concealment is the whole of the difference. Ghostwriting is undisclosed authorship: a document written by somebody whose involvement nobody is told about. Declared writing assistance is a named contribution in the acknowledgements with the funding stated. The ICMJE lists writing assistance among the activities that alone do not qualify somebody for authorship, says such contributors should be acknowledged with their specific contribution described, and advises editors to require that the corresponding author obtain written permission from everybody acknowledged — so the mechanism for doing this properly is published, it is short, and it costs one sentence. Worth noting: the phrase “medical writer” does not appear anywhere in the ICMJE Recommendations, and neither does “ghost”. The term used is writing assistance, and any page attributing those words to the ICMJE is quoting something else."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"cw-3"}><span>{"Can my department head be an author on everything we publish?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"cw-3"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Not on the criteria, and this is worth facing rather than working around. The ICMJE requires all four criteria to be met, and states directly that acquisition of funding, general supervision of a research group and general administrative support do not on their own justify authorship. Criterion 4 is the one that makes it matter rather than merely irregular: an author is undertaking to be accountable for "}<i>{"all aspects"}</i>{" of the work, including ensuring that questions about the accuracy or integrity of any part are investigated and resolved. That is a real undertaking, and signing it for eleven papers a year you have not read is not a courtesy being extended to you. Where a head of department genuinely shaped the question and revised the work critically, they qualify easily and nobody needs to think about it. Where they did not, the honest routes are an acknowledgement, or — better — actually involving them. The qualifier at the top of this page will run any contributor through the four criteria and produce the wording either way."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"cw-4"}><span>{"How do you adapt writing for different audiences?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"cw-4"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"By settling what the reader does after reading, which is a more useful question than who they are. A reviewer decides whether to believe the method, so they need enough method to judge and a claim proportionate to the design. A board decides whether to fund something, so they need the ask and the number in the first paragraph and the methodology in an appendix if at all. A referring colleague decides how to refer, so they need an instruction that survives being skimmed. A patient decides whether to be reassured and what to do next, so they need what will happen, in what order, at a reading level that has been measured rather than asserted. The sample above shows one finding written all four ways. What is not happening in any of them is simplification: the patient version is not the journal version with the statistics taken out, it answers a different question, and writing one and cutting it down produces something that serves neither reader."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"cw-5"}><span>{"Do you guarantee the work will be plagiarism-free?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"cw-5"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"No, because it is not a claim anybody can keep. Nobody can guarantee an absolute of that kind, and the guarantee is worth less than the thing it replaces. What you get instead is an iThenticate similarity report with every match read and classified by a person, which is more useful in clinical writing than any percentage: staging criteria, drug names, standard operative descriptions and instrument names produce unavoidable overlap, and a raw similarity score misrepresents that badly. The question that matters is which matches are boilerplate that no reviewer will object to and which are somebody else’s sentences. We also run AI-content screening and tell you the result rather than only acting on it, because those tools have false positives and you should know what a journal might see."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"cw-6"}><span>{"Can you handle a whole year of a department's output?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"cw-6"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Yes, and it is usually cheaper per document than commissioning them separately, for a reason that has nothing to do with volume discounts. The expensive part of medical writing is not the writing; it is establishing the facts — finding the figure, checking it against source, resolving the two places it is reported differently and deciding which is right. Done once per study, that fact set then supports the paper, the abstract, the poster, the talk, the departmental report and the patient material, and they agree with each other. Commissioned separately over eighteen months by three different people, the same verification is done three times and produces documents that disagree in small ways nobody notices until somebody does. A publication plan also settles the authorship questions once rather than eleven times, which is worth more than it sounds. Where the underlying research is company-sponsored, GPP 2022 governs the publication plan alongside the ICMJE."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"cw-7"}><span>{"What do you do with complex or multidisciplinary material?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"cw-7"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Assign a writer whose field is the one the argument turns on, and bring in a second reader from the other discipline. The failure mode in multidisciplinary writing is not that anything is wrong; it is that each section is written for its own specialists and the document as a whole has no reader. A paper that moves between a surgical technique, a health economic model and a patient-reported outcome instrument needs somebody deciding what a reader of the whole thing needs to carry from one section into the next, and that is an editorial decision rather than a subject one. Practically: one writer owns the through-line, specialists review their own sections, and the second reader is chosen precisely because they are not an expert in all of it — because neither is the reader."}</p></div></div></div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Related services"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Where a specific document has its own page."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Several of the things people ask for here are handled better somewhere else on this site, with their own process and their own sample work."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"rel"}> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"1"}</span><b>{"IF IT IS FOR A JOURNAL"}</b><em>{"papers and cases"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/physician-writing-services/physician-manuscripts/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Physician manuscripts"}</b><span>{"Every manuscript type, and which guideline governs each."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/physician-writing-services/case-report/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Case report writing"}</b><span>{"One patient, written to CARE, with the consent handled first."}</span></a> </div> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"2"}</span><b>{"IF IT IS FOR A READER OUTSIDE MEDICINE"}</b><em>{"patients and the public"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"#/patient-education-content"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Patient education content"}</b><span>{"Written at a reading level that is measured rather than asserted."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"#/physician-training"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Physician training content"}</b><span>{"Education material, and who may actually accredit it."}</span></a> </div> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"3"}</span><b>{"IF SOMEBODY IS SCORING IT"}</b><em>{"funders and reviewers"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/grant-writing/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Grant writing"}</b><span>{"Written to the funder’s scoring criteria, in their order and weight."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/publication-support/responding-to-reviewers/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Response to reviewers"}</b><span>{"Concede, answer or decline — and the third one properly."}</span></a> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Insights"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Further reading on writing for clinical readers."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Three pieces from our library on structure, placement and writing for readers outside the specialty."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"reads rv rv-d1"}> <a className={"read"} href={"https://pubrica.com/academy/physician-writing/how-to-structure-case-reports-review-articles-journals/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How to structure case reports and review articles for medical journals"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Medical journals expect a set structure, with clear objectives and a reporting guideline behind each section."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> <a className={"read"} href={"/insights/how-should-physicians-choose-the-right-journal-for-submitting-a-case-report/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How should physicians choose the right journal for submitting a case report?"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Publishing takes more than clinical knowledge; it demands a strategic read of which journals still publish what, and how."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> <a className={"read"} href={"/insights/how-physicians-can-write-clear-and-impactful-patient-education-materials/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How physicians can write clear and impactful patient education materials"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Patient education materials carry health literacy. Clear ones change adherence; unclear ones quietly cost it."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section section--tight section--dark"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap cta cta__in"}> <div className={"rv"}> <h2>{"Tell us the document and the reader. The rest follows."}</h2> <p className={"lede"} style={{ marginTop: "18px" }}>{"What register it needs, how long it should be, what it will take, and whether the thing you have asked for is the thing that will work — in two business days, at no cost and with no obligation."}</p> </div> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d1"} style={{ margin: "0" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Contact us"}</a> </div> </div> </section> </main>
